#
# Functions of other components the USB HID driver calls: the USB core
# (`usb_v1`) to claim an interface and learn how to open its interrupt pipe, and
# the host controller (`usb_hcd_v1`) to open that pipe and read its reports. The
# driver is a program with no device tree node of its own, so the host
# controller is found by its compatible string, as the USB core does. A pipe is
# the keys `open_pipe` installs in the driver's table, so the functions of a
# pipe (`pipe_v1`) are not listed.
uses usb_v1 via component usb_core { claim_interface, release, interrupt_pipe }
uses usb_hcd_v1 via device compatible "brcm,bcm2708-usb"
{
    open_pipe
}
# In an image with the log server (wood-test), the driver's trace goes to it on
# the interface's io-channel; elsewhere the import stays unlinked and the lines
# wait in the backlog `input_v1.trace` drains.
uses log_v1 via component log_server { flush }
